WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:05.020
The first full trailer for Zack Snyder's Justice
League just dropped and it does a great job

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:07.399
teasing some incredible action scenes.

00:00:07.399 --> 00:00:11.070
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here
and in this video, I'm taking a look at some

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:14.300
interesting details you might have missed
and connections in the trailer to the wider

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.730
DC cinematic universe.

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:19.700
Quick warning: obviously, there's speculation
and potential spoilers ahead for the Justice

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:20.700
League movie.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.220
Let's start with all the hints and teases
in the trailer to the mother boxes, which,

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.911
as we know from the deleted scene in Batman
V Superman, will be key to the plot of the

00:00:27.911 --> 00:00:29.210
Justice League movie.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:33.520
The first mother box appears in a scene with
Silas Stone, the scientist from STAR Labs

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:37.860
who appeared in the metahuman video case file
that Diana Prince, aka Wonder Woman, watched

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:39.230
in Batman v Superman.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:43.510
In that short scene, we saw a motherbox in
STAR Labs react with the amputated body of

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:46.350
Silas's son, Victor Stone, to create Cyborg.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:50.030
Back in the Justice League trailer, it looks
like that motherbox is being activated again

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:54.350
and, as it does so, a Parademon appears just
behind Silas.

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:58.900
And in another shot, it also looks like Cyborg
is carrying or dragging a motherbox beside

00:00:58.900 --> 00:00:59.900
him.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:03.510
By the way, did you notice the football trophies
in this shot which link to the scene later

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:07.000
in the trailer of Silas's son Vic playing
in a football game?

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.250
And that of course fits in with the comics
where Vic Stone was a top football player.

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:15.060
Later in the trailer, there's a scene of the
Apokoliptian army fighting the Amazon army,

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:19.380
and this could be part of the movie's opening
sequence to establish the history of Darkseid's

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:23.260
attempts to invade the Earth and set up the
reasons why he sent Steppenwolf to search

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:24.700
for the mother boxes.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:29.250
The previous Comic Con trailer showed a mother
box being buried, and we know that the Amazons

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:32.700
were given one of the other boxes with the
third going to the Atlanteans.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:37.210
For the third mother box, there's a possible
hint to its location in this underwater shot

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:38.220
of Mera.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:42.340
By the way, in the comics, Mera is the Queen
of Atlantis and Aquaman's wife.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:46.520
Speaking of Aquaman, he gets to do some very
cool stuff in the new trailer, including riding

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:50.909
on the outside of the Batmobile and splitting
the ocean with his trident.

00:01:50.909 --> 00:01:54.369
And I also enjoyed the scene of Bruce Wayne
journeying to the fishing village where we

00:01:54.369 --> 00:01:55.670
see Aquaman.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:02:00.000
These very cinematic shots of a snowy wilderness
are likely footage from the production's shoot

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.250
in Iceland.

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:04.960
The scene with Bruce Wayne meeting Barry Allen
already appeared in the Comic Con footage

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:09.300
released by Warner Bros, but the next shot
is a very cool look at The Flash travelling

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.090
through the speed force.

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:15.919
Notice the incredibly powerful streaks not
only moving around him but also on his suit.

00:02:15.919 --> 00:02:20.180
And according to set visits, the Flash's suit
is wrapped in wires in order to contain the

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:22.430
electricity he generates when he's speeding.

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:26.859
Later in the trailer, we also see a brief
glimpse of Barry's father Dr Henry Allen,

00:02:26.859 --> 00:02:28.109
played by Billy Crudup.

00:02:28.109 --> 00:02:32.440
In the comics and also the TV show, Henry
Allen is imprisoned when he's wrongly convicted

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:34.049
for the murder of Barry's mother.

00:02:34.049 --> 00:02:38.730
Now, the shot you see here is of a tunnel
that was intended to connect Gotham to Metropolis

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:41.279
but was abandoned in the 1930s.

00:02:41.279 --> 00:02:45.030
Set visits have also revealed that this will
be part of a key action scene with Batman,

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:48.420
The Flash and Wonder Woman battling a horde
of Parademons.

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:52.599
The vehicle they're using is also new for
Justice League and it's called the Night Crawler.

00:02:52.599 --> 00:02:56.760
It's an all-terrain vehicle that can move
through all kinds of rough and difficult environments,

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:02.079
and, if you look carefully, you'll see it
forming itself into a kind of spider-tank.

00:03:02.079 --> 00:03:07.209
And in the next shot, it's even climbing vertically
right up the walls of this ventilation shaft.

00:03:07.209 --> 00:03:11.629
We also get to see the new Batmobile in action
and it's been updated since Batman V Superman,

00:03:11.629 --> 00:03:15.719
with the addition of new guns on the front
and sides, plus there's a cannon on top.

00:03:15.719 --> 00:03:20.040
And it wouldn't be a superhero movie or trailer
without a superhero landing, right?

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:24.019
But what I liked about this shot was the visual
similarities with Wonder Woman heading up

00:03:24.019 --> 00:03:27.919
a trio of superheroes, just like she did in
Batman V Superman.

00:03:27.919 --> 00:03:31.459
Some fans might be disappointed that there
was no Superman in this trailer, but we do

00:03:31.459 --> 00:03:36.099
get a shot of Lois Lane as she turns around
to look up at something off camera.

00:03:36.099 --> 00:03:40.280
Which makes me wonder whether that 'something'
will be the Man of Steel making his return.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.159
So, what did you think of the Justice League
trailer?!

00:03:43.159 --> 00:03:47.519
Did it get you hyped for the movie and were
there any easter eggs or things you noticed?

00:03:47.519 --> 00:03:49.469
Let me know in the comments below!

00:03:49.469 --> 00:03:53.379
And if you enjoyed this, I really appreciate
you hitting that like button and why not subscribe

